course: dictionary
lesson: 15193
title: Sedentary
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Sedentary is a long word, but it comes from a simple idea: sitting. It describes things that involve a lot of sitting and very little moving about. «Mia has a sedentary job, so she sits at a desk all day.» Her job keeps her sitting, not moving.
explain: Look for clues around the word. «Too much sedentary time in front of screens can make muscles weak.» Muscles get weak when they are not used, so sedentary must mean not moving much. Try the swap: put "not moving much" in place of the word. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: Sedentary can also describe animals and people who stay in one place. «Sedentary snails stay in the same patch of garden for their whole lives.» Some animals travel far every year, but these never do. In history, a sedentary village is one where people settle down and stay, instead of wandering from place to place.
fact: Sedentary means involving a lot of sitting and very little exercise.
fact: Sedentary can also mean staying in one place, not moving around or migrating.
fact: A sedentary lifestyle means spending long periods sitting, such as long hours in front of screens.
fact: Children are advised to be active for about 60 minutes a day, which is the opposite of a sedentary lifestyle.
fact: Useful phrases: «sedentary lifestyle» and «sedentary job».
exercise: «Tom spends most of the day on the sofa, playing games.» Which word describes Tom's lifestyle? | *Sedentary | Wandering | Speedy | Energetic
exercise: «Sedentary animals stay in one area all year.» What does sedentary mean here? | Hunting at night | *Staying in one place | Moving quickly | Swimming far away
exercise: Which word means the opposite of sedentary, as in a lifestyle full of moving? | *Active | Quiet | Lazy | Still
test: Which sentence uses sedentary correctly? | The sedentary racing car zoomed past the crowd | Ben loves his sedentary dance class on Fridays | The sedentary bird flew south for the winter | *Ben's job is sedentary, so he sits at a desk all day
test: Which of these is a sedentary animal? | A whale that travels across the whole ocean | *A snail that stays in one patch of garden | A salmon that swims upriver each year | A swallow that flies south every autumn
exam: What does a sedentary lifestyle usually mean? | *Lots of sitting and very little exercise | Lots of running and jumping every day | Eating only fruit and vegetables | Living in a tent and moving every week
